Abstract = {Many companies are now increasingly aware of the need to integrate
   digital technologies with ESG aspects. As studies show, companies are
   becoming increasingly aware of the long-term benefits of these
   connections. This study examined whether ESG impacts the relationship
   between enterprise digital transformation and corporate performance.
   This study collected data from Chinese-listed companies in the Shanghai
   and Shenzhen Stock Exchange from 2010 to 2022, which includes 4922
   Chinese listed companies. Using fixed effect method and the generalized
   method of moments as the quantitative analysis approaches. Firstly, a
   positive relationship can be found between enterprise digital
   transformation on corporate performance. This study uses information
   asymmetry to explain why enterprise digital transformation promotes the
   corporate performance. Secondly, this study finds that ESG effectively
   promote the positive relationship between enterprise digital
   transformation and corporate performance. This research enhances the
   understanding of ESG and enterprise digital transformation in relation
   to economic repercussions but also contributes to the affection of
   digital economic transformation on the corporate governance of Chinese
   listed companies. In conclusion, enterprises should strengthen the
   top-level design of ESG construction, establish an effective ESG
   management mechanism, strengthen the recognition of ESG, and constantly
   improve their awareness of ESG information disclosure, which helps
   enterprises improve enterprise digital transformation to achieve
   high-quality development.},
